    description: "Found by the 2026-08-01 directed taint cohort that moved INV-karud from\npending_validation to violated (9 fresh external repos, 321 flows). This item is\nthe concrete fix; INV-karud is the invariant.\n\nROOT CAUSE. io_boundary._module_matches (io_boundary.py:1538) decides whether a\ncatalog entry's module matches an edge's module hint by normalizing :: and / to\n. and then doing BIDIRECTIONAL CASE-INSENSITIVE SUBSTRING matching:\n\n    cm = catalog_module.replace(\"::\", \".\").replace(\"/\", \".\").casefold()\n    em = edge_module_hint.replace(\"::\", \".\").replace(\"/\", \".\").casefold()\n    return cm in em or em in cm\n\nSubstring, not prefix, and not component-aware. 25 of the 210 catalog sink\nmodules are 4 characters or fewer (os, io, fs, net, log, http, sys, std, file,\njson, csv, rpc, ssl, grpc, unix, fmt, ets, Req, Port, Task, File, IO, Deno, Oban,\ndets), so each one matches ANY module whose normalized path merely CONTAINS it.\n\nVERIFIED LIVE (predicate called directly):\n    _module_matches('os',       'chaos')          -> True\n    _module_matches('io',       'audio')          -> True\n    _module_matches('log',      'dialog')         -> True\n    _module_matches('fs',       'dfs.client')     -> True\n    _module_matches('net/http', 'net/http/fcgi')  -> True\n\nOBSERVED ON FRESH SUBSTRATE (8 flows, all Go):\n    caddy         net/http/fcgi Get        -> matched net/http Get            (x2)\n    kserve        net/http/httptest        -> matched net/http NewRequest     (x2)\n                  NewRequest is the TEST request constructor; it performs NO\n                  network IO, so this is a non-realizable network sink.\n    alertmanager  net Close                -> matched net/smtp.Client Close\n    alertmanager  go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/\n                  otlptracegrpc NewClient  -> matched grpc NewClient, because\n                  the module path ENDS in the substring grpc.\n\nWHY THE EXISTING GATE DOES NOT COVER IT. WI-razol's _lookup_named_entry gates two\ncases: a bare ambiguous callee with NO module hint, and a module hint that\nmismatches. But mismatch is decided BY this predicate, so a hint that is present\nand spuriously substring-matches is treated as a match and returns on the first\nhit. The ambiguous_names safety net is only consulted on the no-module-hint path.\n\nWHY IT SURVIVED. Measured on hypergumbo's own tree the fix is clean: 110 flows,\n110 realizable, 0 suspect, with the disambiguation gate exercised 20 times and\ncorrect every time. Every defect above is Go or JavaScript. This is a\nlanguage-coverage gap that only fresh substrate exposes -- which is precisely why\nINV-karud's 2026-06-11 note refused to close on self-tree numbers.\n\nIMPACT, STATED NARROWLY. Within the catalog only ONE name/module pair can flip the\nZONE verdict rather than merely misattribute the primitive: scala run, between\nsys.process.Process (host_fs) and sys.process.ProcessBuilder (subprocess), where\nProcess is literally a substring of ProcessBuilder. The larger exposure is\nover-matching against arbitrary repo module names, which is unbounded.\n\nPROPOSED FIX SHAPE (not implemented; TDD red first). Replace substring containment\nwith COMPONENT-AWARE matching: split both sides on . after normalization and\nrequire one component sequence to be a PREFIX of the other, so net.http matches\nnet.http.Client (type within package) but NOT net.http.fcgi (sibling package), and\nos never matches chaos. The docstring's intended cases must keep working and each\ndeserves a test: Go net.Conn vs net.Conn, Rust std::fs vs std::fs::File, Java\njava.io vs java.io.FileInputStream, and the Swift camelCase-receiver-vs-PascalCase-\ntype cases (Channel vs channel, NonBlockingFileIO vs fileIO) -- note the Swift ones\nare receiver VARIABLE names, so they may need an explicit carve-out rather than\nfalling out of component matching.\n\nCAUTION: _module_matches is shared by io-boundaries and the taint engine, so\ntightening it moves io-boundary counts too. Expect the self-tree validation\nratchet and any io-boundary baselines to shift; re-baseline deliberately (shrink\nonly) rather than accommodating a breach.\n\nREPRO:\n  python3 -c \"from hypergumbo_core.io_boundary import _module_matches; print(_module_matches('os','chaos'))\""  # 90be
